      "writtenOn": "2026-11-01T12:37:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Same issue here, and it can crash: ClearFragment calls this from its lifecycleScope. If Back is pressed while clearing, the scope is cancelled, runCatching turns that into a failure result, and the coroutine carries on to Toast.makeText(requireContext(), ...) on a detached fragment, which throws IllegalStateException (from reading the code, not reproduced). Rethrowing CancellationException here as well fixes it:\n\n```\ntry {\n    programmers.withRemote(...) { remote, session -\u003e remote.programmer.clear(session) }\n    repository.setConfigured(null)\n    Result.success(Unit)\n} catch (e: CancellationException) {\n    throw e\n} catch (e: Exception) {\n    Log.e(TAG, \"Clearing the remote failed\", e)\n    Result.failure(e)\n}\n```",
      "revId": "66c155cfea29a8bea6fa0e87ea527838a5a40454",
      "serverId": "1ec6b3db-b2c1-4fa4-84a2-4c7efe89ba71"
